00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:06.040
Hi!

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:09.250
Thanks for coming.

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:10.540
That's what we promised.

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:15.040
These two are thrilled to see you too.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:23.260
Well, let's get right to it, okay?

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:26.890
Who'd be rude enough to attack you?

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:31.020
The Flash Princess of the Thunder Swirl, 
Elizaveta Fomina.

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:35.440
What excuse has she given for invading?

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:41.200
Elen, please stay calm and listen to me.

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:43.360
It all started during midsummer.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:46.490
Elizaveta and I were working together

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:49.200
to eliminate a band of plundering pirates.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:53.920
Just as we were about to finish things up, 
she sent me a complaint.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:59.090
In it she accused my soldiers of deliberately leading the pirates toward her army.

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:01.590
Did they?

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:04.390
I couldn't tell from the reports.

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:08.100
She broke off contact a few months later.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:11.600
So that's when she started her assault?

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.480
Calling her impatient doesn't even come close.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:20.860
I wish these two would finally see me as unworthy of being a war maiden.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:24.530
If they did, I wouldn't have to ask for your help anymore.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:27.030
But they...

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:29.620
Isn't it great they love you so much?

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.750
You're a war maiden as long as your dragon gear says so.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:35.370
And since I still am, I'm causing you trouble.

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:37.340
Don't worry, Sasha!

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:39.300
Since I'm here, this'll be over soon!

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:42.300
I'll drive that idiot out of Legnica

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.510
and make her kneel before you!

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.180
By the way,

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:52.810
I hear you've been up to some interesting things lately.

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:56.600
Sofy wrote me a letter talking
about how you went to Brune...

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:57.440
I did.

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:59.320
You see, there's this poor, poor guy.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:03.030
I'd feel bad leaving him to
his fate, so I'm helping out.

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:06.070
It seems that quite frequently you're the one being helped.

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:07.870
You talk as if you're any different.

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:11.660
He saved you, didn't he? 
When you had that problem with your breast.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:16.080
You've really taken a shining to that man, haven't you?

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:17.630
He's a fascinating fella.

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:20.340
I bet you'd like him too!

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:21.460
I know!

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:23.090
I'll visit you with him in tow sometime!

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:24.720
You'll have a blast!

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:25.880
It's a great idea, isn't it?

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:28.260
Is it?

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:32.100
Well, I guess I'll have to hold on
a little longer if I want to meet him.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:36.850
A Zhctedian army?

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:42.900
Rumor has it that one of the minor nobles in Brune allied with Zhcted...

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:46.860
They sent several thousand soldiers.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:50.370
Why is he so important to Zhcted?

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:54.000
I've got it!

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.160
Send an envoy!

00:05:56.160 --> 00:06:00.590
If the war maiden with him is as beautiful as they say, I'll offer my support.

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:01.880
Yes, sir!

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:06.050
But if she's not a looker, come back here without doing anything.

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:09.590
First demerit.

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:10.850
Huh?

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:14.100
The first thing you did was thank me for my help.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:15.720
Who says that's why I'm here?

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:19.310
Some people <i>will</i> start making demands if you act like this.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:22.230
But you made tea because we're friends, right?

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:25.940
Sometimes you have to pour a drink for the enemy.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:31.240
If only to throw it in their face should things turn south.

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:32.950
So why are you here?

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:35.790
Make a guess.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:37.200
Want me?

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:43.540
Do you want the help of me and
the four thousand men under me?

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:44.460
I do!

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:45.630
Second demerit.

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:49.380
I know you do, but you shouldn't say it so readily.

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:51.360
It makes you look weak.

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:53.510
Acting so foolish makes me not want to work with you.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.430
Please help me.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:59.190
I've got nothing to pay you with right now,

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:02.770
but if you can wait until the war is over...

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.150
Look at me.

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:11.450
I wonder which is worse: being foolishly honest or simply being a fool.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:15.030
Anyway, I guess you passed the test.

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.120
Then you'll help me?

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:19.000
We've only started negotiating.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:22.000
First, let's talk about what you'll pay me.

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:25.340
When we fought in the Tatra Mountains,

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:29.880
the citadel's gate was destroyed by your troops, remember?

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:33.680
You see, a circular hole was blasted through it.

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:39.520
Despite the fact that gate was made with three steel layers and oak planks between them.

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:43.270
Arifar's not powerful enough for that.

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:45.270
That was you, wasn't it?

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:48.400
Did Eleonora ask you to keep quiet about it?

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:55.410
You won me over with your honesty before.

00:07:55.410 --> 00:08:00.120
I'm hoping to see more of that now.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:01.250
What do you say?

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:10.130
This bow is not exactly what
you'd call a graceful weapon, is it?

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:12.880
It's also a family heirloom.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:14.890
Please stop insulting it.

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:17.680
Why don't you use it more often?

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:20.520
It's on par with dragon gear, after all.

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:23.940
Because I don't understand its power very well.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.270
It also makes me black out occasionally.

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:29.520
Using that bow is a last resort.

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:32.780
I guess you wouldn't want to use it at all in this war then.

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:36.990
When the commander collapses, 
forget fighting forty thousand enemy soldiers.

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:38.870
They'll eat you alive.

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:39.950
And that's how it is.

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:41.620
Sorry to disappoint.

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:43.360
Don't worry.

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:47.060
I'll get a chance to see your power yet.

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:50.300
For now you only have to cover my expenses.

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:54.130
But in return, you'll owe me a favor.

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:05.640
How did things go?

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:07.400
We worked something out.

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:08.860
Glad to hear it.

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:09.520
Likewise.

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:12.940
Though it makes me wonder what makes you so special.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:15.450
Eleonora Viltaria was the first,

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:20.330
but several others have lent you a hand since then. How do you do it?

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:21.450
By being virtuous.

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:25.960
Then I suppose you wouldn't mind helping out another person today.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:28.830
Hey.

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:36.360
You not eating anything is worrying my men.

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:41.350
Careful, it's hot.

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:42.930
Why don't we eat together?

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:47.560
Oh, this is good.

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:52.230
Could I have <i>your</i> soup?

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:55.740
Huh? But I've already started eating...

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:07.500
It's so warm.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:09.960
What's your name?

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:11.750
Regin.

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:13.960
Regin, it's nice to meet you.

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:14.960
I'm—

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:17.340
Tigrevurmud.

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:19.510
Call me Tigre if that's too long.

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:21.970
Tigre...

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:26.230
Anyway, you having eaten takes a load off my mind.

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:27.640
See you later.

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:28.480
Please wait!

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:30.400
What is it?

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:33.520
Can you do me a favor?

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:38.280
My eyes may have different colors,

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:40.910
but both see the same things.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:46.160
Lady War Maiden!

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:50.710
Our scouts spotted a cavalry unit
three thousand strong to the south.

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:52.000
Under what banner?

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:52.670
Two of them:

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:55.670
Crossed swords on a yellow field, and a silver blade on black.

00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:58.630
So you've come, Elen!

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:04.760
The united forces of Legnica and Leitmeritz, led by Elen,

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:07.440
and the forces of Lebus, led by Elizaveta,

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:11.810
are about to clash in Boroszlo, the northeast part of Legnica.

00:11:19.940 --> 00:11:22.070
I want you to protect Elen.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:25.450
Given how long you've been together, I hardly need to ask.

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:28.580
But even so, I want to request it of you once again.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:34.080
I fear Elen has started walking a treacherous path.

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:40.260
There will be people who disagree with her and try to block her road.

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:44.350
When that happens, it won't be her dragon gear that protects her.

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:46.180
It will be people.

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:48.220
People...

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:54.840
You've worked with her as a fellow mercenary even before she became a war maiden.

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:59.230
So I feel I can entrust you with protecting her.

