00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:09.180
Who allowed you to use that name?

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:11.310
Ley Admos!

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:18.150
I wouldn't mind if you called me Liza, Elen!

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:29.320
Putting up a fight will only make this hurt more, Elen.

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:32.450
That's my line!

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:36.960
This is nothing compared to the battles in Brune!

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:40.000
Rise up, soldiers of Legnica!

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:43.710
Make them pay for invading your homeland!

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:51.100
<i>All I can do right now is end this quickly.</i>

00:13:51.550 --> 00:13:52.470
Verni!

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:14.240
That power...

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:18.000
What happened to all the pep you had a moment ago?

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:20.290
Don't boast before you've won.

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:25.960
Tear asunder the air!

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:28.260
Ley Admos!

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:31.680
Fierce claws wrecking Heaven and Earth!

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:33.270
Gron Lazriga!

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:51.780
Seems like we're even—

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:00.920
She pushed me back?

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.750
I guess that settles it.

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:07.840
Not while you still live.

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:11.470
Don't you have more important things to worry about, Elen?

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:15.720
Duke Thenardier and Duke Ganelon

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:18.350
have kept their armies at the ready for a long time now.

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:22.100
Until recently the two of them were simply keeping each other in check.

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:27.730
but it seems as if at least Duke Ganelon
has decided to mobilize his soldiers.

00:15:27.730 --> 00:15:30.280
Though I don't know against whom they're marching.

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:32.660
Ganelon?! Don't tell me you...?

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:34.490
And there's more.

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:39.160
Apparently Muozinel has sent a raiding party of forty thousand to Brune.

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:44.330
Which one of us is pressed for time?

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:45.540
You want my head?

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:48.420
Feel free to keep this up.

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:53.010
But in turn my soldiers are going to keep you busy for a long time.

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:57.260
And if you don't trust me,

00:15:57.260 --> 00:16:00.390
we could always seal a contract.

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:01.520
A contract?

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:06.680
We all withdraw and get back to talking about this business with the pirates.

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:11.210
Let's add a one-year nonaggression pact for good measure.

00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:12.530
What do you say?

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:14.910
Under one condition.

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:16.780
Which would be?

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:19.830
You have to apologize to Sasha.

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:24.540
I won't ask you to grovel—simply be sincere.

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:27.590
Consider it done.

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:37.010
This is how the Battle of Boroszlo came to an end.

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:41.180
The armies walked their own ways to deal with the aftermath.

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:45.650
Due to the gracious offer of the
Legnican soldiers, Elen and her retinue

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:48.150
were able to depart for Leitmeritz the next day.

00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:54.030
<i>Sit tight, Tigre.</i>

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:55.860
<i>Don't do anything rash.</i>

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:57.780
One battle.

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:02.250
That's all we get to defeat the Muozinellan army.

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:03.580
Can we do that?

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:05.040
It's not about whether or not we can!

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:06.880
We've got no choice.

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.040
<i>She's a lot like Elen, huh?</i>

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:09.670
First demerit!

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:11.460
I know you're tired,

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:16.470
but there's nothing to be gained from not paying attention during an important war council.

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:17.430
Sorry.

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:20.010
Should we go over this again?

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:24.270
Your soldiers will only last one more battle, correct?

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:26.440
Not that I can blame them.

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:28.810
This whole operation was reckless to begin with.

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:33.440
You say we'll decide it with the next assault, 
but do you have a plan?

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:37.700
Same thing you did last time, in your fight against twenty thousand soldiers.

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:40.580
When facing an enemy with an
overwhelming advantage in numbers,

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:43.700
you have to either take out their commander or disrupt their supply lines.

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:46.580
The latter's out of the question.

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:49.460
We'd be done in before we could get close to their supply lines.

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:53.380
In other words, Sir Tigrevurmud's bow will decide matters.

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:57.050
It won't be so easy this time.
The enemy's commander is quite skilled.

00:17:57.050 --> 00:17:58.590
You know who leads them?

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:01.050
Kureys Shahin Balamir.

00:18:01.640 --> 00:18:05.100
He's known as Barbaros and is the brother of the Muozinellan king.

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:06.560
Is he famous?

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:08.940
The way she put it makes it seem so.

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:13.780
For crying out loud, has Eleonora taught you nothing?

00:18:13.780 --> 00:18:15.110
Mea culpa.

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:17.400
It was a decade ago.

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:22.450
Sachstein sent a major fleet, 
a full thousand ships, against Muozinel.

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:27.830
But Kureys intercepted them with a mere two hundred ships and prevailed.

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:29.000
He won?

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:30.670
Decisively.

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:33.710
The Sachstein force was helpless before his might.

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:39.380
They nicknamed him Red Beard out of
respect—or Barbarossa in their own tongue.

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:44.510
Later the Muozinellans shortened it to Barbaros.

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:48.560
That's the kind of man we're up against.

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:53.150
Listen closely while I explain our strategy.

00:18:57.850 --> 00:18:58.820
Well?

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:01.700
That might actually give us a chance.

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:03.030
But it's still risky.

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:04.950
Getting cold feet?

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:11.460
Why are you going this far for us?

00:19:12.040 --> 00:19:13.420
It's quite simple.

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:16.210
Because this favor is so huge, 
you'll have no choice but to return it.

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:21.970
I hope you'll satisfy me in your own, unique way.

00:19:22.600 --> 00:19:24.350
I'm already looking forward to it.

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:29.390
After careful scouting by their advance party,

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:32.840
the Muozinellan army is marching straight down the Agnes highway.

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:35.630
The forty thousand soldiers are not moving in a single group,

00:19:35.630 --> 00:19:39.780
but in seven discrete units with a set distance between each.

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:44.070
This allows them to react quickly to surprise attacks while moving.

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:48.200
Red Beard Kureys himself devised this formation.

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:53.960
Well now, I can't wait to see what Zhcted and Brune

00:19:54.370 --> 00:19:56.340
have in store.

00:20:02.890 --> 00:20:04.850
They never showed up, huh?

00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:09.020
The envoy we sent to the 
Zhctedian army has returned.

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:10.850
Oh, took him long enough.

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:15.310
They asked for their message to be delivered orally.

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:17.150
I will repeat it now.

00:20:18.530 --> 00:20:21.570
"We have left our homeland and come here for this reason:

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:25.820
A dignitary of the Kingdom of Brune asked for our assistance.

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:29.550
We have permission to be here, unlike you who has launched a full-scale invasion."

00:20:29.550 --> 00:20:30.290
Huh?

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:33.210
"We have no desire to show ourselves

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:36.920
and actively contend with you, though we will if need be."

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:37.540
And?

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:41.010
"If you return the way you came,
an incident can still be avoided..."

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:41.840
Sure, sure.

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:43.130
That is all.

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:48.220
So what they're saying is 
"turn tail, or you'll get burned."

00:20:49.270 --> 00:20:50.720
You've done well.

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:52.270
You may go rest now.

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:52.980
Yes, sir.

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:58.610
They're right about us being here without just cause.

00:20:58.610 --> 00:21:05.450
The war maiden's accusations of us being invaders are likewise correct,

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:07.700
no two ways around it.

00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:11.450
However, it's one thing for Brunemen to say this

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:14.580
and another for Zhctedians to do so.

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:18.960
If we follow the road, 
we'll pass by two low hills to the west.

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:22.210
The enemy has taken up camp behind the nearer of the two.

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:25.090
We've discovered a group of two thousand people to the northwest.

00:21:25.090 --> 00:21:27.590
They seem to be the slaves
the vanguard had captured.

00:21:28.090 --> 00:21:33.770
We can't run away just because a war maiden threatened us. That'd make for a pathetic excuse.

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:37.520
Come at me, Ludmila Lourie.

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:40.860
We'll see just who'll get burned here.

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:54.200
I'm sure we'll win.

00:21:54.200 --> 00:21:55.370
Simply wait and see.

00:21:58.080 --> 00:21:59.790
Snow has begun to fall.

00:22:00.540 --> 00:22:04.710
It was no longer morning, but not yet noon.

00:22:04.710 --> 00:22:09.530
Soon the battle to be known as the Ormea Campaign would begin.

